  "body": "# Associated User Story\n\nAs an officer, I want to be able to seed the database with an excel sheet or data from get involved - ask further details from Hudson \n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n\n### Officers can import member data by uploading an Excel file or bringing in data from Get Involved, with a preview and confirmation before anything is saved.\n\n**Sunny:** An officer opens the import page, uploads an Excel sheet (or selects Get Involved data), and sees a preview showing how each column matches a field (e.g., name, email, graduation term). They confirm, and the members are added to the database and appear in the members table. The officer sees a summary (e.g., \"48 members added, 2 skipped\"). Existing members are not duplicated, and imported data follows the same rules as normal sign-ups.\n\n**Rainy:** The file is the wrong format, has missing required columns, contains invalid or duplicate entries, the Get Involved data can't be reached, or a regular member tries to import. The system shows a clear error (e.g., \"Please upload an .xlsx file\" or \"Row 5 is missing an email\") instead of failing silently or importing partial or bad data. Nothing is saved until the officer confirms, valid rows can still be imported while problem rows are listed for fixing, and only officers can access the import tool.\n\n# Definition of Done\n\nA story is done when its acceptance criteria are met and every item in the team PR template is satisfied:\n(A) code review by a non-author, coding standard met, RuboCop checked with output/CI link, and setup changes documented;\n(B) the human-only maintainability checks (meaningful comments and names, skinny controllers, thin views, DRY, Rails conventions, foreign keys, enums, nested routes);\n(C) tests added or updated and passing. Any deferred items or RuboCop exclusions are explained in Section D of the PR.",
